          "ImageDescription": {
            "value": "<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Vienna\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Vienna\">Vienna</a>, situated on the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Danube\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Danube\">Danube River</a>, is the capital, largest city, and one of nine states of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Austria\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Austria\">Austria</a>. Vienna was “home” to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Beethoven\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Beethoven\">Beethoven</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Mozart\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Mozart\">Mozart</a>, as well as the world’s first psychoanalyst, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/enSigmund_Freud\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:enSigmund Freud\">Sigmund Freud</a>, and in 2001, the city center was designated a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:World_Heritage_Site\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:World Heritage Site\">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.<br><span style=\"color:blue;\"><i>The <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Scotch_Mist/Poland\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"User:Scotch Mist/Poland\">Scotch Mist Gallery</a> contains many photographs of historic buildings, monuments and memorials of Poland and beyond.</i></span>",
